  "method": "For each fully completed baseline isomer, freeze one approved deterministic ETKDGv3 frame (seed42,100 attempts,1thread,random-coordinate retry only on no conformer). Compare independent isotope-labelled products by full bidirectional chirality-aware substructure isomorphism against direct/mirror products. Corroborate against unchanged f323 canonical mirror-key kernel on identical frozen coordinates; do not consult the new aggregator.",
  "limits": [
    "Groups computed by independent full chirality-aware isotope-product direct/mirror graph matching on frozen frames; corroboration uses the old approved per-isomer kernel, never the new aggregator.",
    "Coordinates are bounded representative structural frames, not an ensemble or rate/temperature model. Native cross-arm pairings may change with frame; never relabel original atoms merely to match a hand partition.",
    "All boron-containing compounds remain ineligible for DP5 scoring. Boron fixtures exercise diagnostic structural topicity only. No UFF/MMFF/model/JVM/GUI work was done.",
    "The eight-form budget remains valid; this work makes no claim for unsupported/enhanced/non-tetrahedral/over-budget cases.",
    "The star example is a valence-valid structural constitution and graph proof, not a literature-verified measured NMR standard. Familiar count-changing methylpentanediol/pentitol fixtures independently cover the requested real-molecule count behavior."
